Ah! I see exactly what’s happening. The extra empty spaces on the left and right are coming from Streamlit’s default column padding and container margins. Even if you set your .chat-box to full width, Streamlit wraps it inside its layout, which adds padding.
To fix this, you need two things:
1️⃣ Override Streamlit container padding via CSS
Add this to your style.css:
Copy code
Css
/* Remove default Streamlit padding for main container */
.css-18e3th9 {  /* Streamlit main container class, may vary by version */
    padding-left: 0rem !important;
    padding-right: 0rem !important;
}

/* Optional: remove padding for columns */
.css-1d391kg {  /* Left column */
    padding-left: 0rem !important;
}
.css-1d391kg + .css-1d391kg {  /* Center column */
    padding-right: 0rem !important;
}
⚠️ Streamlit class names (like .css-18e3th9) can vary with versions. You can inspect in your browser (right click → Inspect → see the container div) and adjust.
2️⃣ Make your chat container full width
In your app.py, update the chat container div:
Copy code
Python
with center:
    # Full width chat container
    st.markdown('<div class="chat-box" style="width:100%; max-width:100%; margin:0; padding:10px;">', unsafe_allow_html=True)

    for s, m in st.session_state.chat_history:
        if s == "You":
            st.markdown(f'<div class="message user">{m}</div>', unsafe_allow_html=True)
        else:
            st.markdown(f'<div class="message bot">{m}</div>', unsafe_allow_html=True)

    st.markdown('</div>', unsafe_allow_html=True)
